# Nix artifacts
#
# Templates ship unlocked so a consumer resolves current nixpkgs on first use,
# and none is re-included below today — the only tracked lock is the root's,
# which belongs to this repo's own flake and not to any template. Locking a
# template means adding `!/templates/<name>/flake.lock` here, and the
# lock-policy check enforces that it agrees with `locked` in
# meta/templates.nix — CLAUDE.md 5.
flake.lock
!/flake.lock

# devenv writes these into whatever directory it runs in, including a template
# directory a maintainer is debugging. .claude/hooks/git-add-before-nix.sh does
# not match a bare `devenv` command, so nothing is staged at that moment — but
# the next nix command in the session stages the whole working tree, and
# .devenv/ holds a live postgres data directory. The test-template skill tells
# you to go poke at a failing copy, so this is not hypothetical.
#
# devenv.lock is the devenv-kind analogue of flake.lock above: ignored by
# default, re-included per template with `!/templates/<name>/devenv.lock` when
# `locked = true` — CLAUDE.md 5.
devenv.lock
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix

result
result-*
.direnv/

.claude/settings.local.json
